# Build context for backend/Dockerfile (T-1104).
#
# The image is built from the workspace that ships with the commit, but only
# the crates, Cargo.lock and the runtime configuration take part in a release
# build. Everything else stays out: a smaller context, and no test corpus,
# fixture or test-only key in the image's history (ASVS V13.4.1, V13.4.2).

# Build output and local caches.
target/
**/target/

# Bench sources and fixture data: never compiled into a release binary (a crate
# that needs a fixture depends on it as a dev-dependency only), and no manifest
# names one, so excluding them cannot break manifest loading.
crates/*/benches/
**/fixtures/

# `crates/*/tests/` is deliberately NOT excluded. `crates/adapters-models/
# Cargo.toml` declares `[[test]] name = "jev"` with no `path`, so cargo resolves
# the file to `tests/jev.rs` while it loads the workspace; an ignored `tests/`
# directory makes every `cargo build -p <svc>` fail on manifest loading before
# it compiles anything. Test sources still never reach the image - the runtime
# stage copies only the release binary (ASVS V13.4.1) - and the policy test
# `crates/api/tests/dockerfile_policy.rs` fails if a manifest-named target is
# added back to this list.

# Coverage and profiler artefacts.
**/*.profraw
coverage/
lcov.info
